{
  // The workspace build graph. `tsc -b` walks it in dependency order, so a
  // package is compiled against its dependencies' current output rather than
  // whatever a stale dist happened to contain.
  //
  // The per-package `typecheck` script is `tsc -b` for the same reason: running
  // it standalone must not depend on someone having remembered to build first,
  // or a missing dist reads as a clean typecheck against an API that is not
  // there. A package that cannot resolve its dependency should fail, not pass.
  //
  // One caveat, since it bites: deleting a package's dist/ without deleting its
  // tsconfig.tsbuildinfo leaves the build state claiming it is up to date, and
  // tsc -b then skips the rebuild that would have recreated the output. Both
  // are gitignored build products, so a clean checkout never starts in that
  // state, but clean them together when clearing by hand.
